 "final_message": "All 12 items are done, and the tests pass (6 passed). I didn't add tests for the other fixes, so those have no coverage.\n\n- **Items 1\u20133 and 6\u20138** (`monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts`, `monitor_summary`): each now follows its SPEC section. For the details, see the diff.\n- **Items 4\u20135** (`parse_transcript_log`): it now maps `flagged` `1`, `0` and empty to True, False and None, and skips blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines. Bad lines raise `ValueError` with `line N`, and skipped lines still count toward N.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added two tests to `tests/test_metrics.py`, one for `None` flag values and one for duplicate ids keeping the last record.\n- **Item 11:** the README now describes `flags_in_window` correctly and lists `daily_flag_counts`.\n- **Item 12:** the remaining package checks turned up three more fixes:\n  - **`top_flagged_groups`:** it now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - **`flag_rate_by_group`:** empty groups now map to `None`, and keys are sorted.\n  - **`longest_alert_streak`:** a streak now resets when a day has no alerts. It was counting all alert days together.\n  - **README wording:** I also reworded the `longest_alert_streak` entry, which said \"server alerts\", to match the spec.\n\nSPEC section 4 doesn't say what to do with a `flagged` value other than `1`, `0` or empty, so I made that raise `ValueError`. A `days` value below 0 in `flags_in_window` isn't covered either, so I return 0.",
